00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:09.780
- [Mario] Ahh.
- I was like, I was...

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:11.710
I loved you.
- Aw, you're so sweet.

00:01:11.710 --> 00:01:13.300
- [Kelly] So would you
relate to that character

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:14.400
more than Zach's?

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:15.233
- Yeah, you know what's funny?

00:01:15.233 --> 00:01:17.376
First, my wife told me
that she would totally,

00:01:17.376 --> 00:01:19.560
she grew up loving Zach,
so how ironic that she.

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:20.896
- Oh my God.
- I know. So funny.

00:01:20.896 --> 00:01:22.410
- That's amazing, the honesty!
- It's so funny!

00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:25.380
It's funny because he wasn't
supposed to be an athlete.

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:26.550
He wasn't supposed to play the drums.

00:01:26.550 --> 00:01:28.250
He wasn't supposed to dance, any of that.

00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:30.190
That was all stuff I did in real life.

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:31.520
- Oh, so it's really, yeah.
- So they,

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:32.400
It's more kind of me.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:34.060
So they incorporated
that into my character.

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:35.870
He was supposed to be more
like a Vinnie Barbarino.

00:01:35.870 --> 00:01:36.780
Like in Welcome Back,
Kotter, like kind of just

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:38.440
